markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Progress Bar Sandbox 



## Option 1: Simple Unit Progress - Manual Fill

**Best for:** super low-maintenance, drop-in everywhere

**How it works:** you copy/paste the same component and just change the percent.


**Total time:** 90 min → percent is “how far through the module you are.”

<div style="max-width:85%; margin:16px auto; background:#f7f8fa; border-radius:12px; padding:12px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
  <p style="font-size:14pt; margin:0 0 8px 0;"><strong>Unit progress</strong> • 35% complete</p>
  <div style="background:#e9ecef; border-radius:999px; height:14px; overflow:hidden;">
    <div style="width:35%; height:14px; background:#0093A4;"></div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:12pt; margin:8px 0 0 0; color:#555;">~32 of 90 minutes</p>
</div>

---

## Option 2: Section “stepper” with time estimates (checks + highlight)

**Best for:** teachers love seeing what’s coming + pacing
**How it works:** a row of “pills” with times. You manually mark completed items with ✅ and highlight the current one.

<div style="max-width:95%; margin:16px auto; background:#f7f8fa; border-radius:12px; padding:14px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
  <p style="font-size:14pt; margin:0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Module roadmap</strong> (90 minutes)</p>

  <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
    <div style="font-size:10pt; padding:4px 5px; border-radius:999px; background:#e4d7f0;">✅ Intro (5)</div>
    <div style="font-size:10pt; padding:4px 5px; border-radius:999px; background:#e4d7f0;">✅ Loops (20)</div>
    <div style="font-size:10pt; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; background:#0093A4; color:white;"><strong>▶ Cards + Loops (20)</strong></div>
    <div style="font-size:10pt; padding:4px 5px; border-radius:999px; background:#ffffff; box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">Filtering + Transparency(15)</div>
    <div style="font-size:10pt; padding:4px 5px; border-radius:999px; background:#ffffff; box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">Copying Data (15)</div>
    <div style="font-size:10pt; padding:4px 5px; border-radius:999px; background:#ffffff; box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">Filtering Data (10)</div>
    <div style="font-size:10pt; padding:5px 5px; border-radius:999px; background:#ffffff; box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">Wrap-up (5)</div>
  </div>
</div>

**Color logic suggestion**

**Completed**: #e4d7f0 (soft purple)

**Current:** #0093A4 (teal)

**Upcoming:** white card w/ subtle shadow

---

## Option 3: 

**Option 3**: Table-style “agenda tracker” (easy to scan)

This would be used at the beginning or end of each section. Or, just an overview at the beginning. 

<div style="max-width:85%; margin:16px auto; background:#f7f8fa; border-radius:12px; padding:14px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
<p style="font-size:14pt; margin:0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Today’s agenda</strong> (90 minutes)</p>
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:13pt;">
 <tr>
      <th style="text-align:left; padding:8px;">Status</th>
      <th style="text-align:left; padding:8px;">Section</th>
      <th style="text-align:left; padding:8px;">Time</th>
    </tr>

 <tr style="background:white; box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
      <td style="padding:8px;">✅</td><td style="padding:8px;">Introduction</td><td style="padding:8px;">5 min</td>
    </tr>
 <tr style="background:white;">
      <td style="padding:8px;">✅</td><td style="padding:8px;">Introducing loops</td><td style="padding:8px;">20 min</td>
    </tr>
 <tr style="background:#e4d7f0;">
      <td style="padding:8px;">⏳</td><td style="padding:8px;"><strong>Displaying objects with loops</strong></td><td style="padding:8px;">20 min</td>
    </tr>
 <tr style="background:white;">
      <td style="padding:8px;">⬜</td><td style="padding:8px;">Filtering and transparency</td><td style="padding:8px;">15 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background:white;">
      <td style="padding:8px;">⬜</td><td style="padding:8px;">Copying data</td><td style="padding:8px;">15 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background:white;">
      <td style="padding:8px;">⬜</td><td style="padding:8px;">Filtering data</td><td style="padding:8px;">10 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background:white;">
      <td style="padding:8px;">⬜</td><td style="padding:8px;">Wrapping up</td><td style="padding:8px;">5 min</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

---

## Option 4: “Learning module sidebar” feel (Levelbuilder-friendly approximation)

This is an attempt to create a sidebar similar to ones in coureses like Coursear. Levelbuilder can't quite capture it. 

<div style="max-width:85%; margin:16px auto; display:flex; gap:14px; align-items:flex-start;">

  <!-- Faux sidebar -->
<div style="width:260px; background:#f7f8fa; border-radius:12px; padding:12px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
<p style="font-size:14pt; margin:0 0 8px 0;"><strong>Module</strong></p>

<p style="font-size:13pt; margin:8px 0;">✅ Introduction <span style="color:#555;">(5)</span></p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt; margin:8px 0;">✅ Loops <span style="color:#555;">(20)</span></p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt; margin:8px 0; background:#0093A4; color:white; padding:6px 8px; border-radius:8px;"><strong>▶ Cards + Loops</strong> <span style="color:white;">(20)</span></p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt; margin:8px 0;">⬜ Filtering + Transparency <span style="color:#555;">(15)</span></p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt; margin:8px 0;">⬜ Copying Data <span style="color:#555;">(15)</span></p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt; margin:8px 0;">⬜ Filtering Data <span style="color:#555;">(10)</span></p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt; margin:8px 0;">⬜ Wrap-up <span style="color:#555;">(5)</span></p>
  </div>

  <!-- Main content placeholder -->
<div style="flex:1; background:white; border-radius:12px; padding:14px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
    <p style="font-size:14pt; margin:0;"><strong>You are here:</strong> Displaying objects with loops (20 min)</p>
    <p style="font-size:14pt; margin:8px 0 0 0;">Use this page to introduce the concept, then move into the practice activity.</p>
  </div>

</div>


